          Basement waterproofing paint has an unfair reputation, and it comes from a single mismatch: people buy it to solve a drainage problem, and drainage problems are not solved with a brush. Used on the wall it was designed for, prepared the way the label demands, a good masonry waterproofer is one of the highest-value things you can do to a damp basement.
        </p>

